            <div xml:id="d744">

                <pb facs="0737" n="725" xml:id="pg725"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.00 Statement July 16, 1937/54: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-29T12:00:00-04:00">July 29,
                        1937—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>115. For the Secretary and Under Secretary. Department’s 62, July 28, 8 p.m. May
                    I be permitted to deny in clearest terms that anything I said to the Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs is susceptible of the interpretation given by him. I have
                    before me the original Spanish text of remarks prepared for use with him
                    immediately before my visit and memorandum of my conversation drafted
                    immediately thereafter and these support my unqualified denial set forth
                    above.</p>
                <p>Furthermore the Spanish text of your declaration which I handed him made your
                    position absolutely clear.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
